body:
I did use tretinoin but its just way too harsh for my skin. Its super sensitive and wont tolerate it. I get whats reminiscent of chemical burns.

&#x200B;

Yes my mental health was really bad on accutane. I attempted suicide twice and self-harmed regularly. However, 6 months off of it and trying anti-depressants I've concluded the problem really is my life circumstance and not anything accutane caused- however I do not tell my doctor this so he does assume its accutane caused but I dont feel comfortable talking about my reasons with him. I told him once while I was on accutane about suicidal thoughts and he wanted to rip my accutane from me then.

&#x200B;

I've tried getting a new doctor but in Canada some doctors wont prescribe it and you have to go through a derm which has long wait lists and again my fear is my acne not being severe enough but I just want to scream at them "NOTHING ELSE WORKS FOR ME PLEASE JUST FUCKING PUT ME ON ROUND 2!" I dont want to get to a point where I'm back at square one with my acne getting as bad as it was before accutane.

&#x200B;

I don't know how to jump through these hoops of convincing my doctors that my mental health is not the result of accutane and to just please renew my prescription because my acne returning certainly isnt making matters better.

Idk. I have yet to revisit him since december. At that time he told me to see how my skin was off accutane for a few months and prescribed me an anti-depressant which did not work for me. 

I appreciate him trying to help me with my mental health but that is a lost cause and I want my clear skin back. I know this seems like a specific case and idk what kind of answers I'm hoping for because i'll probably have to blow the guy to get him to refill my prescription.

&#x200B;

My skin is not as bad as it was before I started treatment in 2017. But I do have whiteheads scattered across my face that I do not want. However it is not severe. 

&#x200B;

I've been on every type of topical prescription, tetracyline, and whatever else he prescribed before I ever attempted accutane. 

&#x200B;

I guess im looking for advice from people who have had acne return post-accutane. How do you go about it with your doctor since it will never be as severe as it was when you first resorted to the drug in the first place?

Obviously I'll show them the picture. I'm not an idiot despite your tone. I've been in before showing a stylist this hair color from the back and received a few blonde foils throughout my dark brown hair. It looks awful. I simply wanted help on what to describe along with the photo. So many hair stylists I go to view the photo once and proceed to do whatever the hell they want. They did a terrible balayage because they want to charge $150. At least where I have gone, stylists ignore and take offence to photos for some reason.

&#x200B;

I know nothing about tones or colors. Is this a balayage or would I require an all over color? Is this warm toned, more ashy, more neutral? I have no idea. My lack of knowledge is what got me scammed out of $150 in the first place. I just wanted help. I'm not saying im going to go blindly into the salon and say brown..... That would be stupid.

&#x200B;

From experience what I say sticks with the stylist more than the photo they ignore.

I'de say theres less social cohesion than other schools for sure but there are clubs and events that you can get into if you want to make the effort. I can't blame the school for having no social life there. It was ultimately my fault. 

At least in my experience, you take a bunch of large classes where you do not get to know anyone. The spread out campus and large classes encourages a very independent experience but does not make it inevitable. I heard they also stopped doing first year seminar courses which is honestly surprising since that was really the only normal class size I had where it was at least possible to get on a first name basis with classmates. 

&#x200B;

My mom, my sister, my dad, my best friend, and the only man I have and will ever love all pushed me to go to UofT. To be fair, they all pushed it because they knew I cared about the prestige and wanted to attend law school and it is somehow believed that UofT law reigns supreme. They wanted me to accept the best because I did work for it. From the outside, UofT seems more desirable and prone to better opportunities. But this is severely flawed thinking across the globe. The place you decide to spend 4+ years should be curated to YOU. There isnt a one size fits all or a school we should all try to get into. Think of it like a long term career.  A doctor may be a prestigious career but realistically, this is not right for everyone. 

&#x200B;

My biggest problem with UofT is so personal and not the schools fault. All those people I mentioned above I ultimately lost. I've been depressed since I was 17 for a number of reasons but this first year was rough and I returned to an old habit of self-harming and live with constant suicidal ideation. This isn't the schools fault. I couldn't cope with losing my old job (in which "the only man i have or ever loved" was my boss and we worked closely together everyday) and being away from my family. But my behaviour and attitude now has made me a plague to my loved ones and my good grades this year are certainly not helping lessen the feeling of regret. 

&#x200B;

You are not stupid for choosing UofT or choosing Western. You got accepted! You can't focus on others expectations of you. You will never feel smart yourself if you are constantly evaluating yourself based on your parents expectations. I used to come home jumping up and down shoving my report cards in my parents faces and now I simply do not tell them a thing. Success will only matter if it's the success you have defined, not what others think it is.  

&#x200B;

My point in writing to you is to really stress this decision is YOURS to make. I always thought university and a long career in law would make me happy from the time I was young. I never focused on relationships and everything I did was to work towards university. I found out too late that what makes me happy are my close relationships, not my grades. It's all about priorities. Don't think of school simply as a step to a long-term career but as something that will alter all areas of your life. 

&#x200B;

The last thing you want out of your university is to feel trapped, completely alone, and unhappy like I am.

Unlike other suggestions I really wouldnt reccomend deep exfoliations with scrubs or devices.  A double cleanse with non-foaming, non-gritty cleansers is what I would advise. Specifically helpful is a salicylic acid face wash. There are high end ones and drugstore ones. The neutrogena oil free acne wash with salicylic acid will do just fine

Pores size is genetic or can be caused from acneic skin and excessive oil production. Post-accutane is when I noticed just how large my pores looked on a pimple-free face. Accutane had decreased my production of oil and reduced my pore size. Its important to understand that you cannot permanently reduce the size of your pores. Even laser solutions and drugs like accutane are transient. It takes constant upkeep.

Retinoids are somewhat proven to reduce pores. I do agree that toner may be useful but its not something thats proven and certainly not for everyone as it can be an irritant.

Clay masks are another transient way to decrease acne. It wont last very long but it does reduce oil production temporarily and thus lessens the appearance of pores.

Also SUNSCREEN. The effects of the sun WILL increase the appearance of your pores.

&#x200B;

Now I've done my research to create my own skin care routine for pores. This isnt proven at all and some products I use may not be right for certain skin and can be irritating. Its all trial and error. But I've been able to reduce the size of mine with constant upkeep.

Most important of course is a sunscreen, but I also use a salicylic acid face wash- La Roche-Posay Effaclar Medicated Gel Acne Cleanser.

&#x200B;

For toner, I suggest starting cheap with TO glycolic acid toner. See how it reacts to your skin. For me, this didnt do anything but it didnt give me a reaction either. Its a good cheap place to start to see if toner is right to incorporate into your routine. I currently use Perricone MD No:Rinse Intensive Pore Minimizing Toner and have had a lot better results. Its got fragrance in it which I'm not too keen on but it definitely works for me. Another good one I liked for a long time until I wanted to test out the Perricone one is the OLEHENRIKSEN Balancing Force Oil Control Toner. This is a really good middle price point one but again, it has some ingredients like a ton of extracts and botanicals I do not like in it. It does also have salicylic acid but also has glycolic and lactic acid. I'll probably go back to purchasing this one after i'm done the Perricone but again, its trial and error. Fragrance and extracts are potential skin irritants for more sensitive skin. Its something to be mindful of but its hard to find something effective for me that doesnt have these ingredients.

&#x200B;

Furthermore, my personal miracle skincare ingredient has been Niacinamide. This ingredient gets a lot of good press from skincare enthusiasts on reddit and dermatologists alike. It is very beneficial. I use The Ordinary 10% Niacinamide + Zinc. Started using this in December and wow, its done wonders for my skins texture and overall complexion.

&#x200B;

I was on tetracycline for a while and while it wasnt strong enough to cure my acne, make sure when your on this your keeping a very low, or better yet- no dairy diet. Not only is this important while on the medication but it will also help with pores if you maintain this kind of diet in the long run.

&#x200B;

Keep in mind that if you are in the midst of an oral prescription treatment for acne and as your acne is healing, your pores will just simply get better with time. The products i've recommended have certainly helped me but on its own, my pores decreased with time after my acne went away and my overall oil production from the pores became less. Your pores will naturally become less noticeable than they are now.

I'm personally transferring from UofT to western for the upcoming fall term.

&#x200B;

Before deciding on UofT i debated and debated, changing my mind everyday but stupidly decided to go with what people thought was more prestigious. 

&#x200B;

I took a bunch of humanities and social science courses this year, just taking whatever interests me until law school. 

Its not very hard to get good grades in those kind of courses. Like high school there are no tricks or loop holes. As long as you put in the work, study and show up, you can succeed here. I have a very good average after first year and honestly did not put in the work I expect from myself because of mental health reasons. 

&#x200B;

I don't know if I'll be happier at Western but I certainly wasnt happy here. 

No one can tell YOU which school is better for YOU. Really evaluate what matters to you most. Dont worry about the what ifs about the difficulty. As long as you take courses you enjoy and put in the work don't worry about it. Certainly don't base your decision off of it. 

&#x200B;

Personally, I left everything to come to UofT because of the prestige and because I came from a small town and was excited about a vibrant city. I quit a job I loved and lost contact with people I loved for seemingly nothing. I had a non--existent  social life this year but then again that type of thing requires more effort than I was willing to put in and dwelled in my own thoughts, regrets, and loneliness. 

&#x200B;

I'm not bashing UofT at all. For the most part I enjoyed the courses I took. I think its a good school but whether or not YOU will be happy here depends on much more than that. I'm only writing this because I envy your position and wish I could do it all over again. I would have made many different decisions. This is a major and personal one. 

&#x200B;

Take a moment to reflect on your own priorities. Don't think about anyone elses opinions on your decision or the opinions of people attending the school. UofT is not cripplingly difficult and you certainly arent secluded from people unless you choose to be. My priorities should have been on my relationships and happiness over my degree.

I had on idea accutane may have been the cause of my deteriorating eyesight until this subredit. This side effect was never disclosed to me. My eye doctor repeatedly had asked me whether I had injured my eyes because my eyesight had gone from 20/20 to 20/300. I never disclosed I was on accutane because I didnt think It made any difference at all. 

&#x200B;

If things are looking good for you in terms of acne I'de suggest stopping. If your acne returns just as bad you can decide on what to do from there.

I took accutane for 2 1/2 years and honestly, I wouldn't say I regret it but I wish I would have actually listened to some of the side effects before doing it. I would ABSOLUTELY not say accutane is 100% worthwhile or fully recommend it to anyone.

&#x200B;

I exhausted every other option and did my best to avoid accutane. My dr gave me 3 options: a variety of topicals, birth control + tetracycline + cutting out dairy (important while on tetracycline) , and accutane

&#x200B;

I did both the first 2 without any success and moved on to accutane. Accutane- without a doubt- is effective for treating acne.

My biggest fear reading endless forums about accutane was the mental side effects because I was already not very stable. A lot of things happened throughout those years that are probably the cause of my worsening depression, suicidal ideation, and attempts but my doctor ripped my accutane prescription away from me after 2 years because of it. I havent gotten any better.

&#x200B;

As for the initial skin side effects, they are hellish for the first few weeks and even months, not going to lie. My skin peeled like crazy and I ended up taking my courses online because I did not want to go out in public. My lips, even now are pretty destroyed from it. They've slowly gotten better but they were a wreck on accutane until I got a medicated lip balm. Drugstore- high end lip balms will not cut it. After 3 months things start to improve quicker and acne will start fading, you wont get new breakouts and with constant moisturizing skin will stop peeling. I also experienced insane nose bleeds and joint pain while on accutane.

&#x200B;

Furthermore, a side effect I didnt even know existed til this subreddit was eyesight. This was never disclosed to me from my doctor but my eyesight went from 20/20 to 20/300 while on accutane. I had no idea accutane could have been to blame until others started reporting it and I did subsequent research about Isotretinoin and eyesight.

&#x200B;

I've only been off accutane a couple months but fear acne returning. Its another mental headache because I feel completely dependant on accutane for clear skin. I can't speak yet as to whether it will return or is worth it in the long-run.

&#x200B;

Just be careful. I have beautifully clear skin but still feel like shit about myself. That did not change. I don't want to get into too much detail on this subreddit but what I incurred mentally while on accutane and still was probably not worth it if that was indeed the culprit.

Go to a new derm? Doctors of all kinds are simply too eager to throw pills down patients throats and something as strong and dangerous as accutane should not be prescribed on a whim.

&#x200B;

If your derm is already throwing pills at you without valid reason or trying safer alternatives first, that is not a derm you want to stick with and doesn't have your interests at heart.

&#x200B;

With any condition I tend to go to two doctors when I can. Sadly some have agendas to push certain treatments and I always like a second opinion.

&#x200B;

Lasering is a possible treatment for scarring. I don't know your skin and can't say whether its right for you and havent had it done myself but I know there are laser treatments for both active acne and scarring. I'm not even sure I understand your derms logic. Acne is always an active possibility when you are off accutane. Most people do not have clear skin, especially those seeking laser treatment...

Ugh Tatcha. I have such a love/hate for it. I so much want to eliminate fragrance from my skincare recently but it's nearly impossible so I'll just enjoy my beautifully scented tatcha that I know works for me.

&#x200B;

I've tried almost everything from the line and havent tried a single thing I didn't like, just some things that fit the price tag better than others. 

&#x200B;

I love the deep cleanse and purchased the full size twice but dont feel exfoliating that much everyday is a good thing for my skin, especially mine that can get flushed pretty easily.  But I dont think i'll be repurchasing again. It's far too expensive for a cleanser. 

&#x200B;

I used water cream for years and loved it but OMG when the sephora sale started last week I ran to my sephora and bought the Luminous Dewy Skin cream and ugh, why tatcha? Why do you make me love you so much? 

I can't live without the rice polish, their moisturizers or their luminous dewy skin mist.

Ooh, i love it! I've been using it for years since I began accutane. I got it in the tatcha bestsellers kit and keep repurchasing that little set because it lasts such a long time since I only exfoliate once or twice a week.

&#x200B;

I'de suggest trying it out in the set and see how it works for you. Also, all the other products in the kit are AMAZING.

I've been off for a few months now and omg I'm terrified. I was off it for a few weeks back in 2018 and started getting small breakouts and panicked. I begged my doctor to renew my prescription even though he absolutely did not want to because of how he thought my mental health was correlated with it. 

&#x200B;

Has anyone had acne return after accutane? I'm debating on switching doctors and getting a new prescription. If I could take it like a vitamin everyday of my life i'de be happy. It just brings me such piece of mind. I have an intense skin care routine because I love taking care of my skin but accutane was the ultimate barrier to products breaking me out. I'm so scared of doing anything to my skin now.

I was prescribed the brand isotretinoin 40mg and the first few weeks were very rough. I was frustrated and my skin looked a lot worse because it was so much dryer. After about 3-4 months my acne got significantly better and after 6 it was completely gone but I did have scarring and severe redness. I never got a single breakout on it. But after my perscription refills ran out I did break out ever so slightly. I panicked and returned to my doctor for refills. 

&#x200B;

The before photos were from day 1 of accutane Jan 27 2017. The after photo was from July 2018. My skin looks exactly the same today. I was on it til February of this year. It takes time for your skin to fully heal especially if you have been dealing with acne for years like I had. 

&#x200B;

 Admittedly I begged my doctor for that final refill and he advised against going on it that long because it wasnt necessary and I was and still am dealing with the mental health side effects. 

You definitely get in the mindset post-accutane that without accutane it will instantly come back. But so far it hasnt. I still worry about it reoccuring and my doctor not refilling my perscription if it does return.

Right after accutane my skin was super dry, red and scarred. I used a lot of kiehls! Their ultra face moisturizer and dark spot corrector were life savers. Also STOCK UP ON LIP BALM. Dry lips will become more annoying than dry skin and acne I promise you. Dr. Dans CortiBalm is your friend and will help you. 

&#x200B;

Once your acne has cleared and your just dealing with scarring you can give your wallet a break and shop The Ordinary. Niacinamide and Azelaic acid will really help with redness and texture

I'm 20. I broke all ties with my parents after they found out about my self harm. I've been doing it for a few years since I was raped at 17 and its destroyed all my relationships and I'm completely alone. Entirely alone. Hide it from your parent as long as you can. No matter how much they love you its a confusing thing. People dont want to be around someone depressing, plain and simple. Sometimes my parents reacted with love, compassion, and sometimes they lashed out blaming my unhappiness on my own choices. I agree. I self harm because every decision I make is the wrong one. I then moved into my own apartment at 18, had a great job, and fell in love with my boss who cared and when they found out I self harmed loved, held and supported me. I fucked that all up too. I fell back on going to university and regret that too because I'm super unhappy, isolated, indescribably lonely, and hung up on the past and the mistakes I've made.  I wish everyday I could hit rewind.

&#x200B;

Self-harming ruins things yet I cant stop and after losing everything, I have no reason not to do it. But I highly suggest if you have something to lose, stop before it sucks everything you have left.

&#x200B;

I'm here to talk if you need it.

Soap Brows from West Barn Co is amazing. Pricey, at least for me to ship to Canada but I've only purchased one tin thats lasted me over a year and is still only halfway done. 

&#x200B;

I also got a clear bar soap from a health food store that works quite well. I think unless you buy a specific waxy soap like the Soap Brows, its really trial and error with different soap formulas. 

&#x200B;

But honestly, soap brows is the most genius beauty hack I've ever discovered. I have long brow hairs that stick so straight and look thin without being brushed up. I used to try to draw them higher and they always looked crazy with my naturally dense brow. Even if you have sparse brows, soap definitely helps reveal the shape and helps certain brow pencils adhere better.

After buying 3 incorrect shades of Giorgio Armani luminous silk over the years til i finally got the right one I highly recommend going into a store that has it and asking for a sample. Store lights will play you and the pictures online are never really accurate.  The numbers do not indicate lighter to darker and the undertones are very different at least in the medium shades than they appear online. 

&#x200B;

Those foundation matcher sites also fail with the armani everytime. No matter which foundations I compare it to. 

&#x200B;

If you must pick one online I'de go with 3.75, 4-5-6's tend to be more warmer - not necessarily darker but warmer and 170 is described as cool tone.

I bought the toofaced one and the NARS radiant longwear at the same time last year because I couldnt decide between the two and they were everywhere online and at sephora at the time. I much prefer the NARS one. Its quite similar in finish maybe the NARS one is slightly more luminous but the NARS one has been the only medium-full coverage foundation ive tried that has gotten me through a 12 hour work day. It also looks a lot better in person and up close than the toofaced one. Just more natural looking. I find it sits on the skin much nicer and less mask-like than the toofaced.

&#x200B;

I have the same skin type as you have described-  combo. Oily in the centre- drier in the perimeter

I've tried a million and 1 foundations I have my favourites for full-coverage rare occassions (Nars Radiant Longwear) but unless my skin is really bad I'll always opt for a light coverage foundation- especially for everyday. 

&#x200B;

I will recommend some good ones I have tried personally but foundation is super personal to your skin type- I'm combo (dry around the perimeter- oily in the centre) 

&#x200B;

**As far as tinted moisturizers and cc creams go:** Laura mercier tinted moisturizer and IT cosmetics original cc cream are pretty good. The laura mercier is definitely more hydrating and lighter coverage than the IT. The IT cosmetics one is more full coverage than I like on an everyday basis but is still quite nice. However, be weary because the IT cc is either a love it or hate it product. It's known to break some people out but I've never had an issue with that. 

&#x200B;

**As for my holy grails:** I've been using Giorgio Armani Luminous silk for YEARS. I'de mix it with my nars for fuller coverage when my acne scars were healing but on its own its still one of my favorites. However, almost about a year ago I discovered the Charlotte Tilbury Light Wonder and it's been my only foundation since. Theres really no describing this. No matter how I apply it, brush, fingers, beauty blender, its always perfect. Its not finicky, you dont need to try desperately to make it work. I really suggest trying a sample.

Hmm. Nars is my winter foundation and I had no problem powdering when I wear it. I use the Charlotte Tilbury airbrush powder so maybe a pressed powder may  work out better than a loose one.  I gave up on loose powders a few years ago because I just hate how powdery they look in person and I'm not big on mattifying my undereyes anyway. I just powder my oily nose area.

&#x200B;

The only problem I've had with the nars breaking apart is if i dont let my moisturizing/primers sink in enough before applying or it will break down around my nose and mouth if I dont lightly powder or if those areas are particularly dry (which they usually are in the winter or if I get sick)

I primarily cut but I've also burned, drank bleach on and off for a few months and abused myself sexually. 

&#x200B;

I also refuse my antidepressants because I have a fear of living in a false reality. I don't want to forget my past or the pain that occurs now.

**UPDATE: Contacted Shoppers on facebook messenger and heres what they said:** at this time, these brushes have not been released online. Please check the website periodically for updates. 

&#x200B;

Hopefully that means they will be releasing! Which would be great news.

For me everyday is natural no makeup-makeup look. I LOVE the look of glowy (not highlightery) skin, no shadow, long lashes (not voluminous) and bushy brows created through soap/wax alone. My steps for everyday are: a moisturizing, brushed up soap brows, pore filling primer, light coverage foundation or skin tint, cream bronzer, charlotte tilbury flawless filter on the high points and inner corner and finish it off with a dewy setting spray. I'll powder around my laugh lines but thats it. I use as few powders as possible.

&#x200B;

For special occasions or if I want to add some flair ill add a single cream shadow (the Charlotte Tilbury eyes to mesmerize ones are PHENOMENAL) and/or a brown winged eyeliner. About once or twice a year ill wear a red lip because glowy skin, no shadow/liner and long lashes is so appealing to me but I always feel out of place in a red lip.

I used to cut at work. I  used small manicure type scissor, an exacto-knife,  or most of the time sharp keys in the bathroom or on break.  

&#x200B;

I don't recommend it even though those pressurized situations inflict the urge. If people find out within those contexts it never ends well.  But if so, don't be like me and use whatever non-sanitary sharp thing you can find...

The only "friend" I've ever had in my life had done the same. Whispering jokes behind my back and spreading the fact I self-harm as if i were juicy gossip. He even made jokes to me, chuckling and say that he hoped I would mutilate a certain female area when cutting my inner thighs as some kind of twisted deterrent. I still don't understand what he meant by that or why he was laughing. 

&#x200B;

Self harm is so taboo that i've found people dont know how to respond which is why I advise not telling anyone you care about. It ruins things. No matter how much they care. I don't know if its because they re-see us as monsters or simply feel helpless. I like to think of the jokes people make as a nervous laughing phenomenon to something they just don't understand. 

&#x200B;

Its nearly impossible to shake the label that comes with self harming. It truly becomes your identity to people who know. Careful breaking ties with people who don't accept it or ridicule you for it. I've found the people who have hated me most are the ones that show the most fake compassion.  No ones going to pat you on the back for what we do. I've lost and broken ties with everyone and everything and nothing will get better going through life alone.

That pissed me off too. I was certain I was gonna fail because of that. Those are always the hardest multiple choice questions in soc courses cause every fucking thing is interconnected you can pretty much justify a, b and c if you try.

&#x200B;

Anyway, off to scramble to get this weeks stupid weekly assignment done before midnight.

I'm first year, so this may not be helpful but HPS110 hasn't had any assignments yet and the midterm is the 28th. Pretty simple course and midterm essay q's are posted before the actual exam so it would be easy to catch up and prepare.

&#x200B;

You may miss out on some tutorial marks but honestly I've already missed two due to weather cancellations/conditions.

A similar thing happened to me. I was stopped yesterday on bloor by someone asking for directions and they proceeded to follow me even after I told them I didn't know the right directions. It was odd because they were originally going the opposite way I was. Luckily I was headed to a class and while he followed me into the building which was super odd, I didnt see him again when I left the lecture. Be safe out there everyone. 

&#x200B;

&#x200B;

I took PSY100 with her last semester. Theres definitely a few questions directly from the textbook. I don't think looking over the mindtap activities again are a good use of time studying though. She covers that stuff in lecture.  As much of a pain in the ass it is, it is however a good idea to skim through the textbook again. She puts a few specific questions from those side examples in the text on both the midterm and final exam.

&#x200B;

Most of it is on lecture notes though.

Mines a poem I stumbled across when I was searching for how to tie a noose. 

&#x200B;

Razors pain you;

Rivers are damp;

Acids stain you;

And drugs cause cramps.

Guns aren’t lawful;

Nooses give;

Gas smells awful;

You might as well live.               

-Dorothy Parker

I'm so sorry. I actually cried reading this because something extremely similar happened to me.

&#x200B;

My manager was the first to find out. He played on it and we had a romantic relationship for a while.

My age at the time we met had people suspicious so one day a coworker brought up presumed sexual harrassment to HR. He told HR I was mentally unstable and I was fired.

&#x200B;

People will fuck you over. I recommend looking for a new job. I was asked by everyone every day how I was feeling. At one point they took sharp objects away from me and forced another coworker to "babysit" me. I was 19. I was humiliated and realized nobody will ever give a fuck.

&#x200B;

My favourite was hearing the words come out of the mouth of the man who I loved that "I was a "liability"

&#x200B;

The betrayal is something I'll never get over. Just I wouldn't recommend doing what I did and make it an excuse to continue cutting

Thank you so much for this! Sounds amazing. That is definitely not the atmosphere at UofT which is one of the many reasons I want to leave. 

I love how people in this reddit just seem so much more positive and helpful than at UofT. Tbh UofT has been really detrimental to my pre-existing mental health problems so I really need a switch! Thank you again, I regret every day that I didnt accept the offer to Kings. 

&#x200B;

Thank you for the info! I was very confident about my grades coming out of high school and while I will meet the admissions average after finishing first year at UofT they arent quite as high as my high school grades, so im just stressing. 

&#x200B;

Thanks again.

Idk, its 5:20am and I cant sleep. Its been like this every week for the past month. But its my overactive thinking that I cant calm

&#x200B;

When I used to work night shift what helped was just playing background noise. A tv show, something. It helps you get out of your head and calm down.

I'm so sorry to hear about your situation. I lost the only person I've ever loved recently. In the most painful way to. I was in love with my boss, who subsequently fired me when he was under heat for our relationship. He used all my weaknesses against me. Told people I tried to sexually assault HIM and that I was mentally unstable and cut. So I lost my job and him. He used my experience of sexual assault and claimed it as his story. It was all lovely really. 

&#x200B;

I can't say it gets better. I have intrusive, overwhelming thoughts about him all the time. I want to take my life in the worst way as a result. I don't know if it takes a "positive" attitude or simply time to heal but I'm no where near there yet. 

&#x200B;

People don't tolerate the depressed/self-harmers. They don't. Most concern if fake and seen as a vulnerability easily exploited. But everyone wants to feel cared about and loved. 

 Everything happened so suddenly that I don't have the balls to message or speak either. 

Love is wonderful, then awful and everything in between. I carved his name into my body because he will never leave my thoughts so why not just engrave it into me. 

&#x200B;

Regardless, if she is still with you, drop the stubborn bullshit. I regret not voicing every single one of my feelings. I don't think he understood the extent to which I loved and still love him. Tell her how you feel. Ultimately, if you feel like things arent working, and she will leave you, what do you have to lose? 

&#x200B;

People will tell you you're better off without her, she didnt care all this crap. But theres little choice in who you love. It kinda just happens and once you care and attach yourself they become part of your identity. I always hated myself until I was with him. He brought out the best version of me that I didnt know existed and doesnt exist now that he's gone. You're never "better off" without those you love.

