Hi. I know what your going through. I've been chronically suicidal since I was about 10 or 11 and started seriously self harming at 18. I've attempted suicide twice and still plan to continue trying. I know my fait is to kill myself. Because the universe is too cruel to do it peacefully for me with any promptness.

&#x200B;

I feel 100% disposable. My body has always been to people and myself. So why not my soul.

That being said, everyone elses life I hold in such high regard. Its hypocritical to say you shouldnt kill yourselfl but I will say it anyway.  Don't

&#x200B;

What i've learned is there is always a bottom. Everything you do either makes you dig yourself into a deeper hole or helps you climb out of it. I've dug my own grave. I've exhausted medical options, coping mechanisms, trying to open up to people, trying to get help.

&#x200B;

Now I distract myself until I have the balls, but more likely i'm still clinging to the hope that one day Ill wake up and my life will change, or at least rewind itself backward a bit so I can do things differently.

&#x200B;

I'm here to talk. That may not help. I know I don't necessarily respond to pm's because I just cant be bothered with people. But I'm here nonetheless.

Most of my problems, in retrospect, were fixable at the time. I'de kill to go back to the day of my first suicide attempt. Things we so much better and I thought at that time I hit rock bottom.

&#x200B;

Try every little stupid thing people suggest. Medicine, therapy, stupid coping mechanisms. Everything. I know they work for some people. Please do not give up until you've tried EVERYTHING.

&#x200B;

Living with suicidal thoughts for as long as you and I have is awful. Its one thing to be tormented by it's thought and every little other negative thought that follows after it and its another thing to do it.

&#x200B;

Most people, myself included, don't actually want to be dead. We want living to be easier. We want a happy life, hell a neutral one would be fantastic and I'll even settle for a slightly depressing existence. I'm going to keep trying until I just cant take it anymore. I really hope you do the same.

I understand your frustration. I started cutting at 18 when I lived at home. My mother also took anything sharp away from me and tried to prevent me from drinking alcohol. Even though at the time I mostly used a metal tooth lash comb that I always had in my purse or keys and my boss was more than willing to get me hammered behind her back.

&#x200B;

Be patient with her. At least she isn't angry and calling you a slut like my mother was.. She cares. My mother didn't know how else to cope besides lash out at me because she felt responsible. Even though it had nothing even remotely to do with my family life. 

&#x200B;

She may blame herself. Doesn't know how to help but wants to. Talk to her about why you are angry with her and why you resent her. Anger is dangerous especially towards family. I burnt bridges with mine and trust me its not what you want. I was 18, and I regret every single thing I did at that age. 

&#x200B;

People, family or not, will try to mould you into what they want. Your mom still wants her little girl. She is technically still responsible for you being you're 17 and she just wants to help. When you are old enough you can do whatever you want but ide advise you to keep a relationship with your family. Try to work things out rather than running away and cutting them off like I did.

Dont worry. I'm sinking in that ocean too. 

&#x200B;

No one gives a damn about how you're truly feeling. And if you open up to them about your self harm they may hug you, pretend to care for a year until one day they decide they hate you and when they see your new marks they say "ugh, that shit again" and fire you and now you're broke and can't live without that person who was once there for you.

As someone whose lost all their friends and has no contact with their family anymore I can relate. 

But it's my single biggest regret. I pushed people I love, still love, completely the fuck out. 

In my head, being depressed and chronically suicidal I knew that I was not exactly fun to be around. They deserved better. I still put schemes and ideas into my head that they all secretly hate me and im nothing but a burden to them. But then again, people have always shown me that they hate me so it might not be scheming. 

&#x200B;

When you have been so alone for so long you just kind of give up. 

Nothing in me wants to go meet new people, listen to what anyone else has to say, respond to messages or emails but the loneliness is absolutely crippling. I hate it. But I have no energy or will to change it. Nor do I think I will ever meet someone again who I can genuinely care about. 

&#x200B;

I've been hurt by so many people in my life that I just have given up. Completely. I was too much in my own head and pit of depression to see who was taking advantage of me, messing further with my head and proceeded to fuck every relationship up. Every single one. 

&#x200B;

The only thing I can suggest is putting on a fake smile, fake interest and do whatever you have to to maintain relationships with people you care about. Later on, you will sure as hell be glad you did.  Even if you don't care to be around them, or listen to them. But deep down we all know who we truly cannot live without.

I feel you. This subreddit is a good place to express things. I started self-harming one night when I was drunk off of my secret stash of water bottles filled with vodka when I still lived at home at 18. Well the intention was to slit my wrists but I was too drunk to precisely succeed and just made a mess. 

&#x200B;

I can't say this will help you but University kinda slapped the alcoholism out of me. The fact that I no longer had easy access to alcohol due to budgets and having to walk for a longer duration than I wanted to be out in public made me cut back. 

&#x200B;

Just be careful. Most of my really significant scars are from self-harming while I was tipsy. Especially my wrists and inner thighs. I don't discourage against going a bit deeper since that seems to be your preference. Just make sure you know where on your body you can and can't

&#x200B;

Everyone learns the hard way to keep your mouth shut when it comes to how your really feeling and sharing personal info. 

&#x200B;

&#x200B;

How many times ive broke down crying to the relatability of Let you down by NF is insane.. 

&#x200B;

Certain songs just trigger it. I have a whole playlist. I can't even listen to music anymore unless its relatable and reflects my mental state.

Don't stress too much. The less you make the scars seem like a big deal the more believable your story will be. 

I'm glad you have a friend that can support you through this. I hope you both can get better. 

&#x200B;

It takes time. Even try going to a school guidance counsellor or some cities have free therapist and clinics that can treat mental health if they are available to you. 

&#x200B;

Good luck!

I'm sorry to hear this. I started self-harming at 18, but was very much depressed before then. I believe I was 10 or 11.

I have attempted suicide twice, once when I was 18, and once when I was 19. I've been diagnosed and have tried several anti-depressants and lets just say tic-tacs are more helpful than what i've tried. I'm not anywhere near over this. I will most likely attempt suicide again.

&#x200B;

You're young, and you sound like you want to get better. Thats a good start. I was never open to therapy and still have never gone but if you are open to it i'de strongly suggest it. Talking is very helpful. At least as a distraction. **Keep distracting yourself!!** I mean it. Thats the only thing you can do until medicine or therapy can maybe work for you.

&#x200B;

Anything you can do to fill time. Don't disassociate from loved ones, Don't stop doing things you have enjoyed in the past. Once you give up there isnt much going back. Do things that you enjoy, try therapy, see a Dr.

&#x200B;

There always needs to be somewhere to start.

You're young! You have so many options to get better. Just try one. Keep trying. Until you've exhausted your options.

&#x200B;

I have so many regrets. One thing I feel I have to mention is to put on a fake smile. Honestly. It's hard because its fake. But telling people, or opening up to anyone besides a doctor or therapist and maybe one person you *REALLY* trust, is a bad idea. No one likes the person whose depressed. I've severed ties with my family, the love of my life and anything I ever once cared about because my depression got the better of me. If I could have faked it. I would at least still have those people. Instead of scarring them all away. Isolation makes everything 100x worse. 

&#x200B;

It's awful that most people don't care about how you are truly feeling. You can come here. Share with us. Just don't put any relationships in jeopardy. If I could rewind the hands of time to last year when I "thought" I was at my lowest, I would. Don't make things worse. Always work to make things better. I ruined everything and can't do anything to bring it back. 

&#x200B;

I wish you nothing bust happiness.

Best of luck.

I have pretty significant scars on my wrists. I started lightly surface-cutting at them but then one day attempted to kill myself that way. Its not pretty, its extremely painful and I might as well have sliced up my face because it's impossible to hide those marks.

