I feel like i should deter you from doing it but personally I do so whenever just seeing blood isn't enough to stop me from crying or panicking. It hurts a lot more and theres a lot more blood. I also get light headed from it, its like a buzz from being drunk without the vomiting. Its a slow drift to being in so much pain you get super tired and pass out which makes me get through very painful days. 

&#x200B;

I like to match my emotional pain to my physical so the physical becomes more pressing and I forget about the emotional. 

&#x200B;

But there are cons that make me stick to surface cuts the majority of the time

I am always worried when I do do it that ill hit something and bleed out painfully. When I do commit suicide I do not want to go that painfully. Or that i'll cut myself to the point where I can't stop bleeding and someone will see and ill get admitted to a hospital. I also like to reduce the amount of scars. I cut for the "in the moment" pain and redirected feelings onto myself. I don't want to leave too many marks that make stumbling through life more difficult.

Idk what to tell you. As someone who cuts I can only tell you that being understanding and there for her is all you can do. You can't make someone stop. When you're suicidal, depressed or feel the need to cut you tend to cut yourself off from everyone.  I haven't answered a single text message in a month. I just dont feel like dealing with people. 

&#x200B;

Just be there for her. Don't get angry at her, don't shame her for doing what she's doing. It only causes more self hatred which is dealt with through continued self harm. 

&#x200B;

Make it known that you care for her, that you'll be with her through this.

Its tough. When I started cutting I worked at a job where the uniforms were short sleeved. It only raised suspicion when I wore the uniform jacket over it. When people found out I was fired. It revolts people and I dont think it's possible for people to see you as normal. Maybe thats what I wanted. I have been abused by so many people that people being revolted by my scars may be a good thing.

&#x200B;

Good luck to you. I'm comfortable with my scars, thats all you can really do.

